course: dictionary
lesson: 12060
title: Making things clear
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Clarifying means making something clearer, so it is easy to understand. When you clarify, you explain a bit more.
explain: «Can you clarify the last step, please?» means: please explain that step again, so I can understand it.
explain: Clarifying can also mean taking the bits out of a liquid so it looks clear, as in cooking. The two meanings are different, so the sentence tells you which one is meant.
fact: Clarifying comes from clarify, which means to make something clear.
fact: Clarifying is the present participle of clarify: clarify, clarifies, clarified, clarifying.
fact: «A clarifying question» is a question that helps make a task or idea clear.
fact: In cooking, «clarified butter» has the white milky part taken out, so it looks clear and golden.
fact: Asking a clarifying question, such as «Do you mean the total or the difference?», can stop mistakes before they happen.
exercise: «Can you clarify the rule for the last game?» What does clarify mean here? | Forget the rule completely | Break the rule into pieces | *Make the rule clearer by explaining it | Write the rule in capitals
exercise: In maths, clarifying the question before you solve it stops mistakes. What does clarifying the question do? | Makes it clearer, so you solve the right problem | Hides the numbers from you | Makes the question longer and harder | *Helps you understand what to solve
exercise: In cooking, «clarified butter» has which part taken out? | The yellow part | *The white milky part | The bread crumbs | The salt
test: Ella asks, «Do you mean the total or the difference?» What kind of question is this? | A question that helps make the task clear | A question with no answer | A question about the weather | *A clarifying question
test: «The teacher is clarifying the rules.» What is the teacher doing? | *Making the rules clearer by explaining them | Breaking all the rules | Counting how many rules there are | Hiding the rules from the class
exam: Ravi asks a clarifying question about the homework. What did his question do? | Ended the lesson early | Was about lunch | Made the homework harder | *Helped make the homework task clear
